-- Reference proof for idem_complement_probe.mm0.  The lan step at l2 binds the
-- rest-binder g = A ∧ B (a NON-minimal ACUI complement): the premise l1 keeps a
-- copy of the principal A ∧ B alongside its decomposition A , B, which is what
-- `finish` needs.  Minimal-complement pinning (g = ∅, premise A , B |- C) hits a
-- dead end (finish cannot fire without A ∧ B present).

idem_complement_probe
---------------------

l1: $ A /\ B , A , B |- C $ by finish []
l2: $ A /\ B |- C $ by lan [l1]
